\subsection{Data Cleaning and Visualization}
After extracting the raw metric data, Microsoft Excel was used for data preprocessing and visualization. For the \textbf{Lines of Code (LOC)} metric, boxplots were generated to visualize the distribution, highlight outliers, and track trends across the five TestNG versions. To reduce the influence of extreme values, cleaned boxplots were also generated by trimming the data to the bottom 90th percentile.

