Under these assumptions, we plot the real-time AoI, the service information update decisions (Update Action), the arrival of information in the AP (Update Arrives@AP), the true capacity of the server ($c_t$@Server), the AP’s observed capacity ($\hat c_t$@AP), and the instant when the client request reaches the AP (Client Req. Arrives@AP). We also annotate the optimal QAoI values, i.e., making the update arrives at AP exactly when the client request arrives at AP.

