\end{tikzcd}
\caption{The $\Ltwo$ de Rham complex in three dimensions (middle), and the finite element subcomplexes of the first (above) and second (below) kinds.}
\label{fig:3DL2deRham}
\end{figure}
\noindent
The top and bottom row of the diagram \cref{fig:3DL2deRham} correspond to the subcomplexes of first and second kinds, respectively.
In particular, $\CG_p$ and  $\DG_p$  denote the usual spaces of continuous and discontinuous piecewise polynomials,
$\Ned_p$~\cite{ned-first-element} and $\NedTwo_p$~\cite{ned-second-element} correspond to the $\Hcurl$-conforming spaces of the first and second kinds, and
$\RT_p$~\cite{rt-element,ned-first-element} and 
$\BDM_p$~\cite{bdm-element,ned-second-element} correspond to the 
$\Hdiv$-conforming spaces of the first and second kinds. One can also form a 
hybrid complex by interchanging kinds as in \cref{fig:3DL2deRham-hybrid}.
