To solve the above problem, we propose the concept of granularity in this audio-driven generation model, which is defined as the number of frames for a complete expressive gesture. We further propose the Multi-Granular Gesture (M3G) framework, which models the motion patterns in different granularities and reconstructs dynamic, holistic body gestures based on multi-granular motion representations.

