We hereby present results of various numerical simulations. In Fig.~\ref{fig2A}(a) we show the dependence of the passive joint angle $\phi$ on time $t$. We used the parameters from Table~\ref{Tab:1} and assumed that the actuation of the simulation is $\psi(t)=A\sin{(\Omega t)}$, with the amplitude of $A=1$ [rad] and frequency $\Omega=1.72$ [rad/s]. The solution is composed of an initial transient which converges to a steady-state periodic solution. It is possible to see that $\phi(t)$ converges to a periodic signal with frequency which equals to the actuation frequency. 

