\section{Complement of the boundary of a polytopal cone as a positivity set}


We consider the following additional consequence of the characterization of polytopal cones that are positivity sets,

\begin{lemma}
Let $C \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{2} $ be a polytopal cone which is the positivity set of a hinge function. Then $(\partial C)^{C}$ is also a positivity set.   
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Since $C$ is a positivity set, by Theorem \ref{thm:main} for the sets 

\[ G = \{ p \in \partial C, -p \in \partial C\} , \quad R = \{p \in C, -p \not \in C\} \]

\[ \langle G \rangle \cap \conv (R) = \emptyset \]

Let $C^{*} = (\partial C)^{C}$. We note that for a polytopal cone $C$, $C^{*}$ is also a polytopal cone and $\partial(C^{*}) = \partial((\partial C)^{C}) = \partial C$. We also have the following sets defined for $C^{*}$

\[ G_{C^{*}} = \{ p \in \partial C^{*}, -p \in \partial C^{*}\}, \quad R_{C^{*}} = \{p \in C^{*}, -p \not \in C^{*}\}   \]

we realize that 

\[ G_{C^{*}} = G \quad R_{C^{*}}, = \{p \in C^{*}, -p \in \partial C \}   \]

We now consider various cases for $\langle G_{C^{*}} \rangle = \langle G \rangle$. 
\begin{case}
 $\langle G_{C^{*}} \rangle = \langle G \rangle = \mathbb{R}^{2}$   
\end{case}
We realize that in this case, as $\langle G \rangle = \mathbb{R}^{2}$, $R = \phi$. Therefore, the polytopal cone $C$ is a symmetric set and as a result $\partial C$ is also a symmetric set and hence $C^{*}$ is also a symmetric set, which implies that $R_{C^{*}} = \phi$. With this we get 

\[ \langle G_{C^{*}} \rangle \cap \conv \langle R_{C^{*}} \rangle = \phi   \]

we use Theorem \ref{thm:main} to conclude that $C^{*}$ is a positivity set.

