For networks $\mathfrak{C}_t, \mathfrak{D}_t$ and $\mS$, we showed that in both scenarios, there is no gain in using these networks multiple times for communication, regardless of the adversarial model. We note that computing the multishot capacities of Family $\mathfrak{A}_t$ and $\mathfrak{B}_s$ relies on new combinatorial techniques, as the one-shot capacities of these networks has yet to be established. Possible research directions in this area include: A scenario where the subset of edges the adversary can attack also changes over multiple uses; calculating the multishot capacity of networks in the general $n$-level network case; calculating the multishot capacity of networks with more than one source.



