    By assigning the tuple $(\ell|_{B_1},\dots,\ell|_{B_{t}})$ to any $\ell\in\mathcal{L}$, we see that $\mathcal{L}\subseteq\mathcal{\hat L}$. The inclusion might be strict if not all constraints of $\B_T$ are inside some $\B_i$. Nevertheless, we know from Claim~\eqref{claim_1628_2211} that those functions $\ell$ that are not homomorphisms yield a trivial contribution to the sum in~\eqref{eqn_1704_2211}. Thus, we can rewrite the sum as
    \begin{align*}
        W_{w,y}
        =\sum_{(\ell_1,\dots,\ell_{t})\in\mathcal{\hat L}}\;\prod_{i\in [t]}Q_{x_i,\ell_i\circ\epsilon_{i,T}}.
    \end{align*}
Now we use that each $\epsilon_{i,T}$ yields an isomorphism from $\A$ to $\B_i$, which gives
\begin{align*}
    W_{w,y}
        &=
        \sum_{\substack{(f_1,\dots,f_{t})\\ f_i:\A\to\Y\;\forall i\in [t]\\f_j(a)=y}}\;\prod_{i\in [t]}Q_{x_i,f_i}
        =      \Big(\sum_{\substack{f:\A\to\Y\\f(a)=y}}Q_{x_j,f}
        \Big)\cdot\Big(\prod_{i\in [t]\setminus \{j\}}\;\sum_{f:\A\to\Y}Q_{x_i,f}\Big)\\
        &=      \Big(\sum_{\substack{f:\A\to\Y\\f(a)=y}}Q_{x_j,f}
        \Big)\cdot\Big(\prod_{i\in [t]\setminus \{j\}}\id_{\HH}\Big)
