\section{Methodology}
In this section, we introduce our method TLJD for city-level FDI prediction in detail. As shown in Figure~\ref{fig:modelstructure}, TLJD consists of two main parts: 1) \textbf{Indicator Feature Encoding} which encodes values of judicial performance indicators as embeddings by transformer layers with arithmetic attention while simultaneously considering both row features and column features; 2) \textbf{City-Level FDI Prediction} which leverages an MoE model consisting of four expert models (i.e., PJ Expert, DJ Expert, JE Expert, and JC Expert) to predict city-level FDIs.
