\section{Background}
In this section, we introduce the background of a recent and influential text-to-image generative model, Stable Diffusion.

Stable Diffusion (SD) \cite{rombach2022high} has emerged as a foundational model in AI-driven art, capable of performing both text-to-image (txt2img) generation and image-to-image (img2img) transformations. Unlike previous models such as Midjourney \cite{midjourney}, SD is fully open-source, including its model architecture, source code, training datasets, research papers, and associated ecosystem. This openness has accelerated the growth of a strong and vibrant ecosystem, encompassing AI art communities, custom-trained AI art models built on SD, and a wide range of auxiliary AI tools and plugins. As a result, SD has not only captured the attention of AI art enthusiasts but has also fostered collaborations between AI professionals and creatives, driving both the development and accessibility of AI-generated content.

The SD model operates through two main processes: the forward diffusion process and the denoising diffusion process. During the forward diffusion process, box noise is incrementally added to an image until it becomes an unstructured noise matrix. In the subsequent denoising diffusion process, this noise matrix is gradually transformed back into a coherent image. This is achieved by predicting and removing noise through a diffusion model, as illustrated in Algorithm \ref{alg:stable_diffusion}. The model is trained to minimize the error between the noise predicted by the model and the actual noise added during each step. By doing so, the diffusion model learns to accurately reverse the noise-adding process, producing high-quality images. This generative approach has made SD one of the most powerful tools for generating realistic and creative images from text descriptions, and its open-source nature ensures its continued evolution and adoption across various applications.

\begin{algorithm}
\caption{Denoising Process in Stable Diffusion Algorithm}
\label{alg:stable_diffusion}
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
\STATE \textbf{Input:} Initial noisy image $x_T$, number of denoising steps $T$, trained model $\epsilon_\theta$
\STATE \textbf{Output:} Generated image $x_0$
\STATE Initialize $x_T \sim \mathcal{N}(0, I)$
\FOR{$t = T, T-1, \ldots, 1$}
    \STATE Sample $z \sim \mathcal{N}(0, I)$ if $t > 1$, otherwise $z = 0$
    \STATE Compute $\epsilon_\theta(x_t, t)$
    \STATE Compute $x_{t-1} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_t}} \left( x_t - \frac{\beta_t}{\sqrt{1 - \bar{\alpha}_t}} \epsilon_\theta(x_t, t) \right) + \sigma_t z$
\ENDFOR
\STATE \textbf{return} $x_0$
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm}
